.TH PROXCHUNK 1 "2026-08-20" "proxchunk 1.7" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
proxchunk \- multi-proxy HTTP Range chunked downloader
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B proxchunk
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.I URL
.br
.B proxchunk
.I URL
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B proxchunk
downloads a file by splitting it into HTTP Range chunks and fetching
those chunks through different proxy IP addresses.
The goal is to reduce the effect of per-IP or per-connection throttling.
.PP
It can fetch public HTTP and SOCKS5 proxy lists, score them, optionally
reuse a local cache, and include local Tor
.RB ( socks5h://127.0.0.1:9050 )
when that port is in use.
The remote server must support HTTP Range requests (206 Partial Content).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIfile\fR
Output path.
Default: last path segment of
.IR URL .
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-concurrent " " \fIN\fR
Maximum concurrent chunk downloads (default: 16).
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-chunk\-mb " " \fIMB\fR
Chunk size in mebibytes (default: 8).
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-proxies " " \fIN\fR
Maximum live proxies to keep (default: 40).
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-refresh " " \fIsec\fR
Background proxy refresh interval in seconds (default: 180).
.TP
.BI \-\-limit\-mb " MB"
Download only the first
.I MB
mebibytes (0 = full file).
.TP
.B \-\-direct
Single-IP download (no proxies).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-progress
Do not draw the TUI progress bars.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-cache
Do not load or save
.IR ~/.cache/proxchunk/proxies.txt .
.TP
.B \-\-show\-proxies
Prefix each chunk bar with a 15-character IPv4 field.
.TP
.BI \-\-socks " url"
Add one extra HTTP or SOCKS proxy.
Repeatable.
Example:
.BR socks5h://127.0.0.1:9050 .
.TP
.BI \-\-proxy\-file " file"
Load extra proxies, one
.I ip:port
or
.I scheme://host:port
per line.
Bare
.I host:port
is treated as HTTP.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-user\-proxies
Do not load
.IR ~/.config/proxchunk/proxies.txt .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-tor
Do not auto-add local Tor on port 9050/9150.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/proxchunk/proxies.txt
Optional user proxy list (ip:port or URL per line).
.TP
.I ~/.cache/proxchunk/proxies.txt
Scored proxy cache from previous runs.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, or help/version requested.
.TP
.B 1
Usage error, probe failure, or download/assemble failure.
.SH EXAMPLES
Download through scored proxies:
.RS
.B proxchunk https://example.com/file.bin
.RE
.PP
Single-IP download with a 32 MiB cap:
.RS
.B proxchunk --direct --limit-mb 32 -o sample.bin https://example.com/file.bin
.RE
.PP
Use a private proxy list:
.RS
.B proxchunk --proxy-file ./proxies.txt --no-cache URL
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR curl (1),
.BR wget (1),
.BR wget2 (1)
.SH BUGS
Free public proxies are often slow or dead.
A stalled chunk is aborted and requeued; if it still fails, the whole
download is not assembled.
There is no resume of a partial output file.
.SH AUTHORS
proxchunk contributors.
